    "specPath": "specs/196-yaml-parsing-moves-off-unsafe-libyaml/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "Every YAML read in the engine (spec frontmatter, compaction plans, the delta classifier, the dependency-only waiver, workflow manifests) goes through `serde_yaml` 0.9, which is deprecated and parses with `unsafe-libyaml`, a c2rust translation of libyaml that RUSTSEC-2024-0449 marks unmaintained. `deny.toml` ignores that advisory by id so `cargo-deny` can pass; this spec removes the reason for the ignore. The engine moves to a YAML crate written in safe Rust, the committed registry and index shard trees stay byte-identical, every refusal the current parser produces on authored frontmatter is kept, and the ignore entry is deleted in the same change.\n",
    "title": "YAML parsing moves off unsafe-libyaml"
  },
